    "https://www.shsu.edu/offices-departments/career-success-center/employer-resources/index.php": {
      "title": "Employer Resources",
      "description": "Employer Resources Skip to main content About Alumni Athletics Giving News Tools & Support Open Search Tools Blackboard Email My Sam SamWeb SHSU Intranet Newton Gresham Library Academic Calendar Site Directory Events Calendar Campus Map Support Academic Success Center Career Success Center First-Generation Center SAM Center Services for Students with Disabilities Student Health Center Student Money Management Academics Academics Where hands-on learning meets real-world skills, success follows. Find what you want to study or explore all your academic opportunities. Majors & Programs Colleges SHSU Online Graduate Studies Honors College Research Admissions Admissions Select the type of student you are to get information on deadlines, requirements, and next steps for applying to SHSU. Freshman Transfer Graduate International SamPoly Accepted Students Cost & Aid Cost & Aid Find out how much it costs to attend SHSU and the variety of financial aid options available to help you pay for it. Cost of Attendance Student Account Services Types of Aid Bearkat Promise Frequently Asked Questions Campus Life Campus Life Explore what it’s like to live on campus at SHSU, from where you’ll live and eat to activities you can take part in outside of class. Housing Clubs & Organizations Greek Life Recreation & Fitness Dining Visit Apply Request Info Tools & Support Open Search Academics Academics Majors & Programs Colleges SHSU Online Graduate Studies Honors College Research Admissions Admissions Freshman Transfer Graduate International SamPoly Accepted Students Cost & Aid Cost & Aid Cost of Attendance Student Account Services Types of Aid Bearkat Promise Frequently Asked Questions Campus Life Campus Life Housing Clubs & Organizations Greek Life Recreation & Fitness Dining Visit Apply Request Info About Alumni Athletics Giving News Back Open Search Tools Blackboard Email My Sam SamWeb SHSU Intranet Newton Gresham Library Academic Calendar Site Directory Events Calendar Campus Map Support Academic Success Center Career Success Center First-Generation Center SAM Center Services for Students with Disabilities Student Health Center Student Money Management Search Keywords Search Employer Resources Your one-stop hub for SHSU employer resources, including recruitment services, sponsorship details, and guidelines for hiring Bearkats on campus and online. Menu Career Success Center news Events Student Resources Student Resources Services Symplicity Job Search Support Resumes & Cover Letters Career & Internship Fairs Career Exploration Assessment Blackboard Learning Lounge Employer Resources Employer Resources Hire a Bearkat Sponsorship Program Policies & Procedures Workshops & Presentations Our Mission people Connect. Recruit. Succeed. Whether you’re recruiting for internships, full-time roles, or building long-term brand presence, the SHSU Career Success Center is here to support you. Below are key tools and services to help you successfully connect with Bearkat talent. Post Jobs & Internships with Ease Our Bearkats Get Hired program makes posting job and internship opportunities fast and effective. You’ll also have access to campus interviews, job fairs, resume referrals, and marketing assistance, all with the support of our Employment Specialists. Learn more on our Hire a Bearkat page. Stand Out with Sponsorship Looking to boost your visibility and make a greater impact? Our Employer Sponsorship Program offers packages that come with premium benefits like featured marketing, social media promotion, priority scheduling, and more. Explore opportunities on our Sponsorship Program page. Know the Guidelines To ensure a smooth and ethical recruiting experience, we ask that all employers review our policies before participating in events or posting jobs. These include our EEO policies, social media and FERPA guidelines, and recruiter expectations. Review details on our Policies & Procedures page. Need Assistance? Our Employer Engagement Team is here to help every step of the way. Whether you're just getting started or returning for another season of recruiting, we’re ready to partner with you. Contact our Employer Engagement Specialist, Jessica Salazar, with questions. jns065@shsu.edu 936-294-1712 Contact the CSC Visit Address: Academic Building IV, Suite 210 1921 Avenue J, Huntsville, TX 77340 Hours: M–F | 8 AM–5 PM Google Maps Link Email careersuccesscenter@shsu.edu Call 936-294-4454 Connect Sam Houston State University 1905 University Avenue Huntsville, TX 77340 936-294-1111 | 866-BEARKAT Policies Employee & Department Search Title IX Site Policies/Additional Links State of Texas Mental Health Counseling Texas Homeland Security TRAIL Fraud Reporting Hotline State Auditor’s Office Hotline Site Directory KatSafe Jobs Open Records Requests The measure of a life is its service"
    },
    "https://www.shsu.edu/offices-departments/career-success-center/employer-resources/hire-a-bearkat.php": {
      "title": "Hire a Bearkat",
      "description": "Hire a Bearkat Skip to main content About Alumni Athletics Giving News Tools & Support Open Search Tools Blackboard Email My Sam SamWeb SHSU Intranet Newton Gresham Library Academic Calendar Site Directory Events Calendar Campus Map Support Academic Success Center Career Success Center First-Generation Center SAM Center Services for Students with Disabilities Student Health Center Student Money Management Academics Academics Where hands-on learning meets real-world skills, success follows. Find what you want to study or explore all your academic opportunities. Majors & Programs Colleges SHSU Online Graduate Studies Honors College Research Admissions Admissions Select the type of student you are to get information on deadlines, requirements, and next steps for applying to SHSU. Freshman Transfer Graduate International SamPoly Accepted Students Cost & Aid Cost & Aid Find out how much it costs to attend SHSU and the variety of financial aid options available to help you pay for it. Cost of Attendance Student Account Services Types of Aid Bearkat Promise Frequently Asked Questions Campus Life Campus Life Explore what it’s like to live on campus at SHSU, from where you’ll live and eat to activities you can take part in outside of class. Housing Clubs & Organizations Greek Life Recreation & Fitness Dining Visit Apply Request Info Tools & Support Open Search Academics Academics Majors & Programs Colleges SHSU Online Graduate Studies Honors College Research Admissions Admissions Freshman Transfer Graduate International SamPoly Accepted Students Cost & Aid Cost & Aid Cost of Attendance Student Account Services Types of Aid Bearkat Promise Frequently Asked Questions Campus Life Campus Life Housing Clubs & Organizations Greek Life Recreation & Fitness Dining Visit Apply Request Info About Alumni Athletics Giving News Back Open Search Tools Blackboard Email My Sam SamWeb SHSU Intranet Newton Gresham Library Academic Calendar Site Directory Events Calendar Campus Map Support Academic Success Center Career Success Center First-Generation Center SAM Center Services for Students with Disabilities Student Health Center Student Money Management Search Keywords Search Hire a Bearkat Connect with SHSU students and alumni by posting jobs, hosting interviews, and engaging on campus, all with personalized support from our team. Menu Career Success Center news Events Student Resources Student Resources Services Symplicity Job Search Support Resumes & Cover Letters Career & Internship Fairs Career Exploration Assessment Blackboard Learning Lounge Employer Resources Employer Resources Hire a Bearkat Sponsorship Program Policies & Procedures Workshops & Presentations Our Mission people Recruiting at SHSU Sam Houston State University offers over 80 bachelor's degrees, 50+ master's programs, and 10 doctoral degrees, including nationally recognized programs in Business, Media, Education, Engineering, Criminal Justice, and more. SHSU is proud to be classified as a Doctoral Research University and a Community Engaged campus by the Carnegie Commission on Higher Education. U.S. News & World Report also ranks SHSU among the top institutions for online graduate programs. We appreciate your interest in our students and are committed to helping you make the most of your recruiting efforts. Our Employment Specialists are ready to assist you with: Campus interviews (in-person or virtual) Information sessions & presentation space reservations Career fair registration & coordination Resume referrals and job vacancy promotion Job & internship postings on Symplicity Campus marketing support Corporate sponsorship opportunities Contact our Employer Engagement Specialist, Jessica Salazar, at jns065@shsu.edu with inquiries. On-Campus Interviewing We offer comfortable and functional recruiting spaces: Multiple private interview rooms A 12-person conference room A 30-seat seminar room Coffee bar, recruiter lounge, and kitchen Complimentary Wi-Fi Support for in-person & virtual interviews To participate in campus interviews, you must be registered with our Bearkats Get Hired sponsorship program. Employer Sponsorship Program Unlock premium services and benefits through our sponsorship packages. Sponsors receive priority support and increased exposure across our platforms. To explore these exclusive opportunities, visit our Sponsorship Program page or contact our Employer Engagement Manager, Audrey Williams, at akw007@shsu.edu . Contact the CSC Visit Address: Academic Building IV, Suite 210 1921 Avenue J, Huntsville, TX 77340 Hours: M–F | 8 AM–5 PM Google Maps Link Email careersuccesscenter@shsu.edu Call 936-294-4454 Connect Sam Houston State University 1905 University Avenue Huntsville, TX 77340 936-294-1111 | 866-BEARKAT Policies Employee & Department Search Title IX Site Policies/Additional Links State of Texas Mental Health Counseling Texas Homeland Security TRAIL Fraud Reporting Hotline State Auditor’s Office Hotline Site Directory KatSafe Jobs Open Records Requests The measure of a life is its service"
    },
    "https://www.shsu.edu/offices-departments/career-success-center/employer-resources/sponsorship-program.php": {
      "title": "Sponsorship Program",
      "description": "Sponsorship Program Skip to main content About Alumni Athletics Giving News Tools & Support Open Search Tools Blackboard Email My Sam SamWeb SHSU Intranet Newton Gresham Library Academic Calendar Site Directory Events Calendar Campus Map Support Academic Success Center Career Success Center First-Generation Center SAM Center Services for Students with Disabilities Student Health Center Student Money Management Academics Academics Where hands-on learning meets real-world skills, success follows. Find what you want to study or explore all your academic opportunities. Majors & Programs Colleges SHSU Online Graduate Studies Honors College Research Admissions Admissions Select the type of student you are to get information on deadlines, requirements, and next steps for applying to SHSU. Freshman Transfer Graduate International SamPoly Accepted Students Cost & Aid Cost & Aid Find out how much it costs to attend SHSU and the variety of financial aid options available to help you pay for it. Cost of Attendance Student Account Services Types of Aid Bearkat Promise Frequently Asked Questions Campus Life Campus Life Explore what it’s like to live on campus at SHSU, from where you’ll live and eat to activities you can take part in outside of class. Housing Clubs & Organizations Greek Life Recreation & Fitness Dining Visit Apply Request Info Tools & Support Open Search Academics Academics Majors & Programs Colleges SHSU Online Graduate Studies Honors College Research Admissions Admissions Freshman Transfer Graduate International SamPoly Accepted Students Cost & Aid Cost & Aid Cost of Attendance Student Account Services Types of Aid Bearkat Promise Frequently Asked Questions Campus Life Campus Life Housing Clubs & Organizations Greek Life Recreation & Fitness Dining Visit Apply Request Info About Alumni Athletics Giving News Back Open Search Tools Blackboard Email My Sam SamWeb SHSU Intranet Newton Gresham Library Academic Calendar Site Directory Events Calendar Campus Map Support Academic Success Center Career Success Center First-Generation Center SAM Center Services for Students with Disabilities Student Health Center Student Money Management Search Keywords Search Sponsorship Program Support SHSU students while promoting your brand. Our sponsorship program connects employers with talent through events, outreach, and recognition. Menu Career Success Center news Events Student Resources Student Resources Services Symplicity Job Search Support Resumes & Cover Letters Career & Internship Fairs Career Exploration Assessment Blackboard Learning Lounge Employer Resources Employer Resources Hire a Bearkat Sponsorship Program Policies & Procedures Workshops & Presentations Our Mission people Connecting Employers & Bearkats The Career Success Center launched a new initiative in 2023 to take a more proactive, personalized approach in connecting employers with SHSU students and alumni. Personalized Recruitment Support We now offer a concierge-style service for employers seeking to recruit Bearkat talent. Our Employer Engagement Team works closely with each organization to help identify and connect with the right candidates. There are numerous packages available to fit your needs and budget. To learn more, contact Audrey Williams, Employer Engagement Manager, at akw007@shsu.edu or call 936-294-2535. Sponsorship Benefits Various benefits are exclusive to, or available across all packages. We’re happy to offer a free consultation at your earliest convenience to discuss any questions! Job & Internship Postings Target specific majors & student groups. Social media promotions for 6,200+ combined followers. Promote openings exclusively to students & alumni through Blackboard & LinkedIn . Spotlights on television displays located in our lobby and office, Symplicity CSM is now available! Tabling Spotlights Reserve indoor or outdoor spaces to promote company career opportunities. Tabling events will be promoted through social media & web platforms. On-Campus Events Meet with students & alumni at Career and Internship Fairs . Sponsor a table at our annual Etiquette Dinner. Host on-campus information sessions. Be highlighted or speak during our Career Education & Development (UNIV 2112) course. On-Campus Interviews Reserve up to 4 office spaces. Conduct interviews with students & alumni. Promote your interviews through email blasts & social media promotions. Branding Opportunities Advertise your company to students through social media, website spotlights, email, and on-campus television displays. Have content designed by our Marketing Coordinator distributed digitally & in-person. Have your company logo printed on our merchandise and swag items. Exclusively at SHSU Connect through platforms made by us and available ONLY to SHSU community members. Platforms Include: Bearkats Get Hired: A dedicated LinkedIn group where employers post openings & network with Bearkats. Blackboard Learning Lounge : Automatically available each semester, this virtual space includes a virtual job board with listings categorized by: On-campus jobs All-majors opportunities College-specific postings Contact the CSC Visit Address: Academic Building IV, Suite 210 1921 Avenue J, Huntsville, TX 77340 Hours: M–F | 8 AM–5 PM Google Maps Link Email careersuccesscenter@shsu.edu Call 936-294-4454 Connect Sam Houston State University 1905 University Avenue Huntsville, TX 77340 936-294-1111 | 866-BEARKAT Policies Employee & Department Search Title IX Site Policies/Additional Links State of Texas Mental Health Counseling Texas Homeland Security TRAIL Fraud Reporting Hotline State Auditor’s Office Hotline Site Directory KatSafe Jobs Open Records Requests The measure of a life is its service"
    },
    "https://www.shsu.edu/offices-departments/career-success-center/employer-resources/policies-procedures.php": {
      "title": "Employer Policies & Procedures",
      "description": "Policies & Procedures Skip to main content About Alumni Athletics Giving News Tools & Support Open Search Tools Blackboard Email My Sam SamWeb SHSU Intranet Newton Gresham Library Academic Calendar Site Directory Events Calendar Campus Map Support Academic Success Center Career Success Center First-Generation Center SAM Center Services for Students with Disabilities Student Health Center Student Money Management Academics Academics Where hands-on learning meets real-world skills, success follows. Find what you want to study or explore all your academic opportunities. Majors & Programs Colleges SHSU Online Graduate Studies Honors College Research Admissions Admissions Select the type of student you are to get information on deadlines, requirements, and next steps for applying to SHSU. Freshman Transfer Graduate International SamPoly Accepted Students Cost & Aid Cost & Aid Find out how much it costs to attend SHSU and the variety of financial aid options available to help you pay for it. Cost of Attendance Student Account Services Types of Aid Bearkat Promise Frequently Asked Questions Campus Life Campus Life Explore what it’s like to live on campus at SHSU, from where you’ll live and eat to activities you can take part in outside of class. Housing Clubs & Organizations Greek Life Recreation & Fitness Dining Visit Apply Request Info Tools & Support Open Search Academics Academics Majors & Programs Colleges SHSU Online Graduate Studies Honors College Research Admissions Admissions Freshman Transfer Graduate International SamPoly Accepted Students Cost & Aid Cost & Aid Cost of Attendance Student Account Services Types of Aid Bearkat Promise Frequently Asked Questions Campus Life Campus Life Housing Clubs & Organizations Greek Life Recreation & Fitness Dining Visit Apply Request Info About Alumni Athletics Giving News Back Open Search Tools Blackboard Email My Sam SamWeb SHSU Intranet Newton Gresham Library Academic Calendar Site Directory Events Calendar Campus Map Support Academic Success Center Career Success Center First-Generation Center SAM Center Services for Students with Disabilities Student Health Center Student Money Management Search Keywords Search Employer Policies & Procedures Understand SHSU’s employer policies, expectations, and ethical guidelines for recruiting Bearkats through our events, job board, and campus engagement. Menu Career Success Center news Events Student Resources Student Resources Services Symplicity Job Search Support Resumes & Cover Letters Career & Internship Fairs Career Exploration Assessment Blackboard Learning Lounge Employer Resources Employer Resources Hire a Bearkat Sponsorship Program Policies & Procedures Workshops & Presentations Our Mission people Ensuring a Fair Hiring Experience The Career Success Center follows the NACE Principles for Professional Practice, ensuring ethical conduct by employers, students, and career services professionals. Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Sam Houston State University and the Career Success Center are committed to equal opportunity and non-discrimination in employment. Employers using our services must comply with federal and state regulations governing employment practices in Texas. Learn more at the Texas Workforce Commission . For guidelines on pre-employment inquiries and citizenship, visit the EEOC website . Social Media Policy By posting positions through our sponsorship program, employers grant SHSU permission to promote those positions on official Career Success Center social media channels. To opt out, email our Employer Engagement Specialist, Jessica Salazar, at jns065@shsu.edu . Student Information & FERPA All student and alumni data is protected under FERPA. Resume books and referrals are accessible only with student/alumni consent and must be used solely for hiring purposes within your organization. More info: U.S. Department of Education FERPA Guidelines Recruitment Restrictions & Policies SHSU’s employer services primarily support direct-hire positions with salary or hourly compensation. Not permitted to recruit or post positions: Multi-level marketing (MLM) companies Employers requiring upfront purchases Commission-only roles (unless clearly disclosed) Third-party recruiters must: Disclose the employer they represent Confirm applicants will not be charged any fees Career Fair Policies Cancellations & Refunds Refunds available before the event deadline (see event registration form) Requests must be submitted in writing on company letterhead Option to apply your payment to a future event Refunds are processed through SHSU’s Business Office Late Arrivals & No-Shows Call 936-294-4454 if running late Unnotified late arrivals may forfeit their table to walk-in employers No refunds for no-shows Table Assignments Assigned based on display needs, recruiter count, and competing organizations Tables are not shareable Requests to move must be approved by the Employer Engagement Manager or Director On-Campus Interviews Eligibility: Only direct-hire organizations recruiting for internships or degree-required roles may conduct interviews. Process: Contact our Employer Engagement Specialist at 936-294-1712 Interviews are scheduled through our sponsorship program Employers must follow EEO laws and NACE standards Open and pre-select scheduling options available Interviews conducted Mon–Fri, 8:30 AM–5:00 PM during fall/spring semesters Cancellations: Employers must notify us promptly of any changes to their schedules to minimize student disruption. Note: The Career Success Center reserves the right to decline participation to any employer not aligned with these policies. Contact the CSC Visit Address: Academic Building IV, Suite 210 1921 Avenue J, Huntsville, TX 77340 Hours: M–F | 8 AM–5 PM Google Maps Link Email careersuccesscenter@shsu.edu Call 936-294-4454 Connect Sam Houston State University 1905 University Avenue Huntsville, TX 77340 936-294-1111 | 866-BEARKAT Policies Employee & Department Search Title IX Site Policies/Additional Links State of Texas Mental Health Counseling Texas Homeland Security TRAIL Fraud Reporting Hotline State Auditor’s Office Hotline Site Directory KatSafe Jobs Open Records Requests The measure of a life is its service"
    },
    "https://www.shsu.edu/offices-departments/career-success-center/workshops-presentations.php": {
      "title": "404 Page Not Found",
