    "https://www.shsu.edu/hiring/index.php": {
      "title": "Join the Bearkat Team!",
      "description": "Join the Bearkat Team! Skip to main content About Alumni Athletics Giving News Tools & Support Open Search Tools Blackboard Email My Sam SamWeb SHSU Intranet Newton Gresham Library Academic Calendar Site Directory Events Calendar Campus Map Support Academic Success Center Career Success Center First-Generation Center SAM Center Services for Students with Disabilities Student Health Center Student Money Management Academics Academics Where hands-on learning meets real-world skills, success follows. Find what you want to study or explore all your academic opportunities. Majors & Programs Colleges SHSU Online Graduate Studies Honors College Research Admissions Admissions Select the type of student you are to get information on deadlines, requirements, and next steps for applying to SHSU. Freshman Transfer Graduate International SamPoly Accepted Students Cost & Aid Cost & Aid Find out how much it costs to attend SHSU and the variety of financial aid options available to help you pay for it. Cost of Attendance Student Account Services Types of Aid Bearkat Promise Frequently Asked Questions Campus Life Campus Life Explore what it’s like to live on campus at SHSU, from where you’ll live and eat to activities you can take part in outside of class. Housing Clubs & Organizations Greek Life Recreation & Fitness Dining Visit Apply Request Info Tools & Support Open Search Academics Academics Majors & Programs Colleges SHSU Online Graduate Studies Honors College Research Admissions Admissions Freshman Transfer Graduate International SamPoly Accepted Students Cost & Aid Cost & Aid Cost of Attendance Student Account Services Types of Aid Bearkat Promise Frequently Asked Questions Campus Life Campus Life Housing Clubs & Organizations Greek Life Recreation & Fitness Dining Visit Apply Request Info About Alumni Athletics Giving News Back Open Search Tools Blackboard Email My Sam SamWeb SHSU Intranet Newton Gresham Library Academic Calendar Site Directory Events Calendar Campus Map Support Academic Success Center Career Success Center First-Generation Center SAM Center Services for Students with Disabilities Student Health Center Student Money Management Search Keywords Search Join the Bearkat Team! Explore opportunities to grow your career at Sam Houston State University. Search Jobs Menu Join the Bearkat Team! Living Here Why SHSU? Living in Huntsville Living in Conroe Living in The Woodlands Prospective Faculty HR News and Reminders People Operations Sam Houston State continues to earn national recognition for excellence and opportunity. Money Magazine named Sam Houston one of the Best Colleges in America, a distinction held by only 700 of more than 2,400 universities. U.S. News & World Report placed us among the top 15% of universities nationwide and top 20% of public schools. Explore Opportunities At SHSU, we offer a wide range of employment opportunities for individuals at every stage of their career. Whether you're a seasoned educator, a skilled professional, or a student looking for part-time work, there's a place for you here. Faculty Positions Shape the future by teaching and mentoring the next generation of Bearkats. Staff Positions Support the university’s mission through roles in administration, operations, and services. Executive Staff Charter Schools Join our affiliated charter school teams and help deliver innovative K–12 education in a supportive, mission-driven environment. Student Workers Join departments across campus in flexible, skill-building roles designed to complement your academic schedule. Apply for a Job You can apply for faculty, staff, and student positions online! Faculty, staff and student positions are posted on PeopleAdmin. If accommodations are needed to complete the application process, please contact Human Resources by emailing employment@shsu.edu or calling 936-294-1070. How to Apply Found an open position? Create an account to apply online and track the status of your applications. Faculty positions are posted for 10 business days. Exempt Staff positions are posted for 10 calendar days Non-Exempt Staff for 5 calendar days. Positions may be posted longer based on the needs of the hiring department. For SHSU Employees - Create an account in PeopleAdmin (Faculty, Staff & Student) Getting Hired Application Screening Your application is immediately accessible by the hiring department upon submission. Hiring departments review applications for minimum qualifications and rank candidates to determine who they would like to interview. If not selected, you will receive a notification when the position is filled. The length of the hiring process can vary based upon the needs of the individual hiring departments. Interviews The hiring manager will call to conduct a phone interview and/or schedule an interview. If your interview is in-person, ask the hiring department about parking or visit the parking website here . Again, the interview process can vary based on upon the needs of the hiring department but the process will be consistent between applicants applying for the same position. Background Check If you are a finalist, Human Resources runs a background check to ensure eligibility of employment. All information obtained through a criminal background check is privileged and confidential and will not be released or disclosed to any unauthorized person. Offer If selected, the Hiring Department calls to offer you the position with a hiring salary and start date. Some departments may extend an offer prior to a background check. All offers are contingent on a successful background check. Hiring Paperwork If you accepted our offer, Human Resources emails you hiring paperwork to be completed electronically through Adobe Sign. To avoid unnecessary delays in hiring or receiving your first pay check, complete paperwork immediately upon receiving. Begin Work Your hiring paperwork must be complete before you can begin working. Human Resources will notify you when you are eligible to begin work. Faculty and staff are invited to new hire orientation to review benefits and procedures. Are You a Veteran? If seven or fewer applicants are chosen for an interview, a qualified veteran’s preference applicant from the pool must be interviewed. If more than seven are interviewed, 20% of the number interviewed that are qualified veteran’s preference applicants must be interviewed. We also encourage veteran applicants and employees to use our campus Veteran & Military-Connected Center. What's EEO? Sam Houston State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer and Smoke/Drug-Free Workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, creed, ancestry, marital status, citizenship, color, national origin, sex, religion, age, disability, or protected veteran status. The University takes seriously the initiative to ensure equal opportunity in the workforce and to comply with Title VII as interpreted by the U.S. Supreme Court. Sam Houston State University is an \"at will\" employer. Employees with a contract will have additional terms and conditions. Security-sensitive positions at SHSU require background checks in accordance with Education Code §51.215. Security & Fire Safety at Work Sam Houston State University is committed to the safety of our university community. Each year, SHSU releases an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report to provide information about local crime statistics, safety policies, and the preventative measures in place to protect our faculty, staff, and students. You can view the report online, download a copy of it, or request a hard copy from the University Police Department. The non-emergency phone number for the University Police Department is 936.294.1800 . For SHSU Employees - Read Annual Security & Fire Safety Report News & Reminders The latest updates from human resources. Teleworking Changes - 9/01/2025 The Texas Legislature recently passed two bills which impact Telework opportunities and procedures at SHSU (HB 5196 and SB2615). These laws clarify which employees are eligible for telework and require written telework agreements which may last no longer than one year. The University has approved updating policy HR-17 and telework forms to ensure compliance as of 9/1/25. For more information, please attend the 8/28/25 Webinar, or watch the recording in Talent Management. Employee Emergency Fund (EEF) The Employee Emergency Fund (EEF), designed through Staff Senate and administered by People Operations (PO), is a donation-based fund that considers requests for a one-time payroll payment of $500.00 for full-time, benefits-eligible Sam Houston State University (SHSU) employees who experience qualifying pressing financial need. Free Mental Health Resources Did you know that SHSU’s medical insurance plan offers mental health virtual visits at no cost? Health Select covers visits through Doctor on Demand by Included Health and MDLIVE at 100% for enrollees. Get additional employee mental health resources through the Employee Assistance Program (EAP). All employees and their dependents may access multiple mental health counseling sessions at no cost. Username and password for the EAP website are SHSU or employees may call 800-346-3549. • Health Select and Consumer Directed Health Select provides more services. Please visit Blue Cross Blue Shield of Texas, Health Select Website. For information regarding your current benefit elections, please contact 936-294-1070, or email us at hrbenefits@shsu.edu. Power of your Benefits! Explore your comprehensive earnings at SHSU with our new Total Estimated Compensation tool. Holidays Sam Houston State University provides paid holidays to employees to help balance work and family responsibilities. Employees may observe alternative holidays in lieu of a university holiday. Eligibility Benefits-eligible staff, with an FTE greater than or equal to .5, are eligible for paid holidays. Academic year faculty/academic staff, temporary employees (including students), and part-time employees who work irregular schedules are not eligible for paid holidays. Those not eligible should refer to the academic calendar for holidays. For SHSU Employees - Academic Calendar Holiday Schedule Below is the holiday schedule for fiscal year 2026. Labor Day September 1, 2025 Monday Thanksgiving November 27, 2025 Thursday Thanksgiving November 28, 2025 Friday Skeleton Crew Days * December 19, 2025 Friday Winter Break December 22, 2025 Monday Winter Break December 23, 2025 Tuesday Winter Break December 24, 2025 Wednesday Winter Break December 25, 2025 Thursday Winter Break December 26, 2025 Friday Winter Break December 29, 2025 Monday Winter Break December 30, 2025 Tuesday Winter Break December 31, 2025 Wednesday Winter Break January 1, 2026 Thursday Winter Break January 2, 2026 Friday Skeleton Crew Days * January 5, 2026 Monday Skeleton Crew Days * January 6, 2026 Tuesday Martin Luther King Jr. Day January 19, 2026 Monday Skeleton Crew Days * March 11, 2026 Wednesday Skeleton Crew Days * March 12, 2026 Thursday Skeleton Crew Days * March 13, 2026 Friday Memorial Day May 25, 2026 Monday Emancipation Day June 19, 2026 Friday Skeleton Crew Days * July 3, 2026 Friday *During skeleton crew days, administrative and other offices noted in policy HR-08 remain operational with limited staff. For SHSU Employees - FAQs: Holiday and Skeleton Crew Days Alternative Holidays The following alternative days may be observed in lieu of a university holiday. Employees will need to discuss with their supervisor about availability of the desired date to switch. The total number of holidays in a year to which an employee is entitled is not changed by use of alternative holidays. Rosh Hashanah September 23, 2025 Tuesday Rosh Hashanah September 24, 2025 Wednesday Yom Kippur October 2, 2025 Thursday Good Friday April 3, 2026 Friday Living Well At SHSU Sam Houston State University recognizes a great work-life balance is essential to living a happy, healthy life and optimizing employee performance. Explore many resources and perks we offer to our employees. Insurance Medical Coverage The Employees Retirement System of Texas (ERS) is the administrator for Texas Employees Group Benefits Program (GBP) which provides health and other optional coverage to insurance eligible employees and their eligible dependents. Employees can choose to enroll in either HealthSelect of Texas or Consumer Directed HealthSelect Plan. Dental Coverage Employees can choose to enroll in one of two dental plans. State of Texas Dental Choice Plan is a preferred provider organization dental insurance plan or DeltaCare USA dental HMO, which is a dental health maintenance organization dental insurance plan. Vision Coverage Employees can choose to enroll in the State of Texas Vision. For a set copay amount, the plan offers and eye exam, contact lens fitting, and an allowance for the cost of eyeglasses or contact lenses and discounts for LASIK. Long-Term Disability Long-term disability provides 60% of the employee’s monthly salary with benefits payable until the employee returns to work or until employee reaches Maximum Benefit Period (based on the age disabled) or based on the condition causing disability. Must complete the 180-day waiting period or use all available sick leave (including extended sick leave, donated sick leave and sick leave pool), whichever is longest. Short-Term Disability Short-term disability provides 66% of the employee’s monthly salary with benefits payable for a period of up to five months (a maximum of 150 days) after completion of a 30-day waiting period or use all available sick leave (including extended sick leave, donated sick leave and sick leave pool), whichever is longest. Life Insurance (AD&D) Voluntary Accidental Death and Dismemberment (AD&D) provides additional financial support if employee or eligible dependent has an accidental injury or death. Amount chosen can be in increments of $5,000 starting at $10,000 up to $200,000. Optional Life Insurance Optional Term Optional Term Life Insurance provides additional coverage, including AD&D coverage, up to four times your annual salary (Election 1, 2, 3 or 4). Maximum coverage is $400,000. Dependent Term Life Insurance Dependent Term Life insurance provides the employee to have $5,000 life insurance, including AD&D for eligible dependents. For SHSU Employees - More about insurance Wellness Employee Assistance Program (EAP) EAP services are available to faculty and staff employees and employees’ immediate families to help resolve issues related to family, mental health, finances, legal concerns, and alcohol and drug problems. The EAP provides counseling and support for all types of life concerns. Elevate Program Elevate is the SHSU Healthy Campus initiative to prioritize the health and wellness of students, faculty and staff. Paid Time Off Benefits eligible employees may be granted paid time off for wellness activities, vacation, illness, injury, and pregnancy. Fitness Center The Department of Recreational Sports and Activities offers a wide variety of recreational programming and provides facilities for students, faculty and staff. Mother's Rooms Mother’s Rooms are available across campus, providing a private place to nurse, pump, bottle feed, and change a diaper. Nursing mothers will need to contact the department or area monitoring the room for access. If you are unsure of who to contact, ask us! Linkedin Learning As an employee, you have access to the Linkedin Learning library that contains wellness related video courses. Once logged in with your SHSU credentials, you can connect your Linkedin profile. For SHSU Employees - More about Programs Financial TRS - Teacher's Retirement Plan Employees contribute 8.25% and the State contributes 8.25% of the employee’s wages. Employee contributions are tax deferred. Interest is credited annually on August 31st to the member’s account. Members vest after 5 years of credible service. ORP – Optional Retirement Plan Employee contributes 6.65% and the State contributes 6.6% of the employee’s wages. Employee contributions are tax deferred. These contributions are deposited with the employee’s selected ORP carrier. Participants vest after one year and one day of ORP participation. ORP is a defined contribution plan with benefits based upon individual investment decisions. For SHSU Employees - Retirement Longevity Pay Additional compensation based on the employee’s total lifetime State of Texas service. Longevity is paid only to full-time staff and is calculated at the rate of $20 per month for each two years of lifetime service credit, up to a maximum of 42 years of service. Compensation Hazardous Pay. Commissioned law enforcement officers or custodial officers are eligible for hazardous duty pay of $10 a month for each 12 months of lifetime service credit. For SHSU Employees - Compensation Discount Programs Employees are encouraged to use discount programs that provide savings on technology, entertainment, travel, and more. For SHSU Employees - Programs Flex Spending Account Flex Spending Accounts allow employees to set aside money from their paycheck, pre-tax, to pay for eligible health and dependent day care expenses. This reduces the employee’s taxable income, resulting in lower federal income tax payments. For SHSU Employees - Insurance Grow Tuition Assistance Program Eligible employees can work and earn an SHSU degree at a discounted rate. For SHSU Employees - Programs Linkedin Learning As an employee, you have access to the LinkedIn Learning video library, where you can learn and improve job-related skills. Once logged in with your SHSU credentials, you can connect your LinkedIn profile. For SHSU Employees - Linkedin Learning The Learning Academies The Learning Academies offer both live and online classes that feature competency-based curriculum. We have multiple professional development tracks, designed to meet specific needs. For SHSU Employees - See Tracks & Schedule Trainings & Conferences Employees are encouraged to take advantage of training opportunities on and off campus. Staff are required to earn professional development credit each year. For SHSU Employees - Learn & Develop Library The Newton Gresham Library primarily serves the research needs but is also available to you for self-growth and leisure reading! The library holds over 1.3 million books, bound periodicals, and government documents. For SHSU Employees - Library Community Organizations Employees can participate in the Faculty Senate or Staff Council depending on their position type. These organizations are motivated to enhance work culture and discuss relevant issues. For SHSU Employees - Learn more about organizations Employee Resource Groups Sam Houston State University will allow for the formation of Employee Resource Groups (ERGs) by current employees to network and promote awareness, and respect at the University. For SHSU Employees - Learn more about ERGs Sam Houston State University 1905 University Avenue Huntsville, TX 77340 936-294-1111 | 866-BEARKAT Policies Employee & Department Search Title IX Site Policies/Additional Links State of Texas Mental Health Counseling Texas Homeland Security TRAIL Fraud Reporting Hotline State Auditor’s Office Hotline Site Directory KatSafe Jobs Open Records Requests The measure of a life is its service"
    }
